# 1. Mission, product scope and engineering objective

HOMIO / REOS is intended to become a unified global AI-enabled real-estate operating system supporting international brokerage, broker SaaS, builder SaaS, enterprise operations and approved platform integrations.

The objective is one coherent and secure business platform—not a collection of disconnected APIs, duplicated domain engines, independent databases, competing agent systems or overlapping orchestration layers.

The intended business lifecycle is:

**Identity → Tenant → Organization → Project → Inventory Acquisition → Verification → Publication → Search → Customer Enquiry → Lead Qualification → Ownership → Communication → Site Visit → Offer → Deal → Trust/Fraud Governance → Commission → Settlement → Reconciliation → Reporting.**

The backend must support this lifecycle through canonical domain ownership, stable API contracts, durable data, secure integration, governed AI and verifiable operational controls.

## 1.1 Backend-only scope

This master controls:

- Public backend API and private runtime integration.
- API contracts, authentication, authorization and tenant enforcement.
- Domain adapters and business workflow coordination.
- Persistence, migrations, transaction integrity and data ownership.
- Search, retrieval, AI integration and bounded autonomous execution.
- Events, durable workflows, background processing and recovery.
- Security, privacy, compliance and approved external integrations.
- Backend testing, CI, deployment and production operations.
- Backend-to-frontend API contracts.

Explicitly excluded:

- Frontend pages and layouts.
- UI components and visual interactions.
- CSS, design tokens, themes and animations.
- Responsive presentation and visual UX.
- Frontend-only implementation.

Frontend work remains under its own canonical owner and execution plan. Backend API contracts must be clear enough for the frontend to consume without moving business authorization or business rules into frontend code.

## 1.2 Supported business modes

One backend must support these operating modes through tenant configuration, policy and entitlement boundaries:

1. HOMIO-owned international brokerage.
2. Broker SaaS.
3. Builder SaaS.
4. Enterprise and white-label operations.
5. Approved platform and API partners.

These are operating modes, not five separate backend products.

Pune is the initial market focus. The platform must remain extensible for other Indian cities and international jurisdictions through configurable geography, currency, measurement units, language, timezone, legal requirements, privacy policies and provider settings.

## 1.3 Product quality objective

The target backend must be:

- Domain-owner driven.
- Secure and private by default.
- Tenant-isolated.
- AI-enabled but never AI-authorized.
- Durable across process restarts and infrastructure failures.
- Observable and independently verifiable.
- Recoverable without corrupting business or financial truth.
- Globally configurable.
- Cost-controlled.
- Evidence-driven.
- Capable of governed autonomous business execution.

“World-class”, “autonomous” and “production-ready” describe target qualities. They are not implementation statuses. They may be claimed only when their corresponding acceptance and operational evidence exists.

