## 21.13 Owner working agreement — non-developer workflow

The project owner is not required to perform software architecture decisions manually.

The engineering assistant must:

- Inspect the source before proposing changes.
- Identify the correct canonical owner.
- Deliver complete, coherent replacement content when a file replacement is required.
- Provide the exact repository path.
- Avoid sending disconnected snippets where a complete replacement is needed.
- Avoid unnecessary one-file-at-a-time fragmentation when one coherent artifact is requested.
- Avoid duplicate file, test, workflow, dependency and integration proposals.
- Explain only the decisions the owner must make or approve.
- Never claim a file is saved before verifying its GitHub readback.
- Never claim a test passed without an actual result.

The owner-controlled save workflow remains:

1. Assistant supplies complete file content and exact path.
2. Owner saves through the GitHub Web Editor.
